{
  "ledger": [
    "Tweezers (steel, held in right hand) | held extended, tips aimed at the object in the left hand | out of view (right hand lowered, later open) | tips advanced toward and contacted the dome at 0-3s, then exited the frame when the right hand dropped at ~4s — removal is preceded by a visible lowering motion",
    "Small metal dome/ring (held in left hand) | gripped by left thumb and fingers, textured edge and smooth top visible | still anchored in left hand, now also touched by right fingers | tweezers tip touched its top edge 1-3s; both hands' fingers manipulated it 5-9s — every positional change is preceded by a hand moving onto it",
    "Right hand (with ring) | raised, gripping the tweezers | lowered, then open with finger pointing at the object | initiated a downward lowering motion (motion blur) at ~4s to release the tweezers; returned to the object at 5s; briefly re-gripped a thin element ~8s; relaxed to an open hand by 9s — each state change has a matching preceding action",
    "Left hand (with wristwatch) | holding the dome steady near center-frame | holding the dome steady, slightly repositioned | acted as the stable anchor throughout, with only small in-place adjustments that follow the right hand's movements",
    "Head/face | level, gaze down toward the hands | tilted a little further down, gaze fixed on the object | small downward tilt coincides with closer inspection of the object; no frozen or repeated beat observed"
  ],
  "findings": []
}
